WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:10.231
<b>Most of the work I put off isn't complicated.</b>

2
00:00:10.231 --> 00:00:11.399
<b>It's just scattered.</b>

3
00:00:11.983 --> 00:00:14.027
<b>ChatGPT Work helps me pull it together.</b>

4
00:00:14.485 --> 00:00:17.196
<b>Before we dive in, let's talk about the difference</b>

5
00:00:17.196 --> 00:00:18.740
<b>between Work and Chat.</b>

6
00:00:19.115 --> 00:00:22.368
<b>Chat is great when I need a thoughtful answer.</b>

7
00:00:22.535 --> 00:00:25.955
<b>Work goes a step further: it can bring in information</b>

8
00:00:25.955 --> 00:00:27.665
<b>from the apps I already use</b>

9
00:00:27.665 --> 00:00:29.751
<b>and help me actually finish the task.</b>

10
00:00:30.251 --> 00:00:33.004
<b>I need to confirm a team dinner next week,</b>

11
00:00:33.004 --> 00:00:35.757
<b>but the restaurant's email is buried in my Gmail</b>

12
00:00:35.757 --> 00:00:37.091
<b>and the latest headcount</b>

13
00:00:37.091 --> 00:00:39.135
<b>and dietary restrictions are in Slack.</b>

14
00:00:39.719 --> 00:00:40.928
<b>The details are split,</b>

15
00:00:40.928 --> 00:00:42.555
<b>between my inbox and Slack</b>

16
00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:44.932
<b>and I don't want to dig through both</b>

17
00:00:44.932 --> 00:00:46.684
<b>just to send one reply.</b>

18
00:00:46.684 --> 00:00:50.355
<b>First, I'm going to download the ChatGPT desktop app.</b>

19
00:00:51.064 --> 00:00:55.443
<b>You can also use Work mode on the web at chatgpt.com,</b>

20
00:00:55.526 --> 00:00:57.904
<b>but the app makes it easy to work alongside</b>

21
00:00:57.904 --> 00:01:00.073
<b>everything else I already have open.</b>

22
00:01:00.365 --> 00:01:02.617
<b>I'll open the download page,</b>

23
00:01:02.617 --> 00:01:04.744
<b>choose the version for my computer,</b>

24
00:01:04.744 --> 00:01:06.996
<b>and follow the installation steps.</b>

25
00:01:06.996 --> 00:01:09.749
<b>Now I'll open the app and sign in</b>

26
00:01:09.832 --> 00:01:12.460
<b>with the ChatGPT account I want to use.</b>

27
00:01:12.543 --> 00:01:16.881
<b>Once I'm in, I can choose between Chat and Work.</b>

28
00:01:16.881 --> 00:01:19.133
<b>Chat is where I go for a quick question.</b>

29
00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:22.053
<b>For this, I'm selecting Work mode</b>

30
00:01:22.053 --> 00:01:24.806
<b>because I want ChatGPT to find information</b>

31
00:01:24.806 --> 00:01:28.518
<b>in Gmail and Slack and then use it to draft an email.</b>

32
00:01:28.518 --> 00:01:32.355
<b>To find that email, ChatGPT needs access to Gmail.</b>

33
00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:34.565
<b>That's where plugins come in.</b>

34
00:01:34.565 --> 00:01:38.653
<b>Plugins connect ChatGPT to the apps I already use,</b>

35
00:01:38.653 --> 00:01:42.365
<b>like Gmail, Slack, Calendar, and Google Drive.</b>

36
00:01:42.698 --> 00:01:45.034
<b>I'll click Plugins in the sidebar,</b>

37
00:01:45.493 --> 00:01:48.496
<b>search for Gmail, and select Install.</b>

38
00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:52.875
<b>Then I'll sign in and review the permissions</b>

39
00:01:52.875 --> 00:01:54.419
<b>before connecting my account.</b>

40
00:01:54.419 --> 00:01:56.087
<b>I only need to do this once.</b>

41
00:01:56.504 --> 00:01:58.756
<b>I'm also connecting the Slack Plugin,</b>

42
00:01:58.756 --> 00:02:02.218
<b>so now ChatGPT can pull the restaurant's email</b>

43
00:02:02.218 --> 00:02:05.054
<b>and the latest team details into the same place.</b>

44
00:02:05.263 --> 00:02:08.933
<b>Now I'll start a new chat and switch to Work mode.</b>

45
00:02:09.475 --> 00:02:12.019
<b>I'll explain what I need: find the email,</b>

46
00:02:12.562 --> 00:02:15.064
<b>check Slack for the latest team details,</b>

47
00:02:15.064 --> 00:02:16.858
<b>and draft a reply.</b>

48
00:02:17.108 --> 00:02:20.278
<b>I can let ChatGPT gather the information it needs,</b>

49
00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:22.113
<b>but I still want to review the draft</b>

50
00:02:22.321 --> 00:02:23.739
<b>before anything gets sent.</b>

51
00:02:23.823 --> 00:02:25.700
<b>You don't need a perfect prompt.</b>

52
00:02:25.783 --> 00:02:27.952
<b>Just ask ChatGPT for what you want!</b>

53
00:02:28.244 --> 00:02:31.372
<b>All right, it's finding the restaurant email in Gmail</b>

54
00:02:31.372 --> 00:02:33.499
<b>and checking Slack for our latest headcount</b>

55
00:02:33.499 --> 00:02:35.042
<b>and dietary restrictions.</b>

56
00:02:35.334 --> 00:02:37.753
<b>If it needs more information or permission,</b>

57
00:02:37.753 --> 00:02:41.257
<b>it can ask me. Otherwise, I can let the task finish</b>

58
00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:43.134
<b>and come back when it's ready.</b>

59
00:02:43.217 --> 00:02:44.552
<b>Here's the restaurant email</b>

60
00:02:44.635 --> 00:02:46.929
<b>asking me to confirm Thursday at seven,</b>

61
00:02:47.013 --> 00:02:48.473
<b>and here's the Slack update</b>

62
00:02:48.556 --> 00:02:51.392
<b>with the final headcount and dietary needs.</b>

63
00:02:51.392 --> 00:02:53.519
<b>And this is the part that actually helps.</b>

64
00:02:53.769 --> 00:02:56.814
<b>It pulls the details together from both apps</b>

65
00:02:56.814 --> 00:02:58.316
<b>and gets the reply ready.</b>

66
00:02:58.566 --> 00:03:00.026
<b>I'll read through the draft</b>

67
00:03:00.109 --> 00:03:01.861
<b>and make one quick change:</b>

68
00:03:01.944 --> 00:03:04.697
<b>ask for a quiet table, if one is available.</b>

69
00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:07.700
<b>When I'm happy with it, I approve the send.</b>

70
00:03:07.783 --> 00:03:09.702
<b>Nothing goes out until I say so.</b>

71
00:03:09.744 --> 00:03:12.788
<b>One more thing – I'm going to wake up my pet.</b>

72
00:03:12.872 --> 00:03:15.124
<b>This gives me an easy way to notice</b>

73
00:03:15.124 --> 00:03:17.877
<b>when Work finishes something or needs my attention.</b>

74
00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:19.962
<b>It's also adorable.</b>

75
00:03:19.962 --> 00:03:23.633
<b>I'll open the menu, search for Wake Pet, and turn it on.</b>

76
00:03:24.175 --> 00:03:26.761
<b>Now I don't have to sit here watching</b>

77
00:03:26.761 --> 00:03:28.721
<b>the conversation while something runs,</b>

78
00:03:28.721 --> 00:03:31.140
<b>and I'll get an alert when it's finished.</b>

79
00:03:31.432 --> 00:03:33.684
<b>This setup works for all sorts of tasks.</b>

80
00:03:34.018 --> 00:03:36.145
<b>I can follow up on an overdue email,</b>

81
00:03:36.354 --> 00:03:37.605
<b>pull in a Slack update,</b>

82
00:03:37.605 --> 00:03:39.815
<b>or find the file I need for a meeting.</b>

83
00:03:40.024 --> 00:03:42.944
<b>I started with Gmail, but the real advantage</b>

84
00:03:42.944 --> 00:03:46.531
<b>is having my email, messages, files, and calendar</b>

85
00:03:46.531 --> 00:03:48.407
<b>together in one place.</b>

86
00:03:48.658 --> 00:03:50.952
<b>Look at us, getting things done.</b>

87
00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:52.870
<b>That's ChatGPT Work.</b>
